A||||7||Ed||V-6 Engines from ARI||||1||
Z||000000||Ed||12-24-2001||02:23 PM||||Someone suggested looking at <A HREF="http://www.engine-parts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.engine-parts.com</A>   for V-6 kits and engines. <P>They have a full line of V-6 stuff, and they even talk about Fieros!  Anyone here used their stuff?  I wonder about their 3.4L, as they bore out the Fiero 2.8L block.  That's an attractive alternative to modifying a Camaro engine.  But I understand boring out a 2.8L to make 3.4 liters is not a good idea.  An e-mail from ARI in response to my question on this subject said that their engine is strong, reinforced, and guaranteed.<P>Anyone here had any first-hand experience with this or other companies which bore out the 2.8L to convert it to 3.4L?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Patrick's Dad||12-24-2001||02:32 PM||||I see them constantly pitching their short blocks on eBay for $1100, but I never see takers.<P>My impression on boring the 2.8 block is the same; that's why GM recast it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FormulaJoe||12-24-2001||04:30 PM||||You can bore a 2.8 out and stroke it to make a 3.4 but you need to make sure the cylinder walls are a minimum thickness.  That is why they do an ultrasound on the block to make sure they have no core shift.  I am thinking the reason they get few takers on ebay is people probably contact them directly.  Besides what they do is nothing special, there are at least half a dozen places here in Indy that will do the same thing for you, for about the same cost and you dont have to pay shipping if you get it done local.  Check with some local engine rebuilders and see what they would charge to do the job, most large cities have engine rebuilders.<P>------------------<BR>Yellow Formula<BR>(soon to be 3.4 DOHC)||||reg||6
Z||000003||voyagerspe||12-24-2001||06:50 PM||||Ive got there 3.4 in my 87 GT.<P>Its a great engine, ARI is a great company to deal with.  We have talked about them before (you can do a search for more info)||||reg||7
Z||000004||FieroRacer||12-24-2001||11:38 PM||||I think there are no takers because their ebay start prices are equal to their web site's prices.  At least for their 3.1 Stroker kit.  If they want e-bayer's to bite, they have to start below their listed price.||||reg||1
Z||000005||AkursedX||12-25-2001||12:46 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroRacer:<BR><B>If they want e-bayer's to bite, they have to start below their listed price.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>But it's an easy way to get cheap advertising.  That is probably the main reason they put their auctions up.  I'm sure many of us in the Fiero community would have never heard of them if they didn't put their auctions up there<P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||gtsonly||12-25-2001||06:59 PM||||I have read where you can only bore a 2.8 out to a 2.9 safely! Anything more and you run the risk of cracking the block! Is this true?||||reg||1
Z||000007||GT GT 87||12-25-2001||07:56 PM||||I hope everyone realizes to get 3.4 it is by using a 3.1 crank plus a bore job ! I've got a 3.2------Slight bore job with a 3.1 crank.||||reg||1
